{"h":3395,"lines":[{"x":0.13168724238150639,"t":"Test 3","y":0.097383720787522332,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944611,"w":0.057613169352213556},{"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","y":0.14098837195714176,"x":0.13168723657386514,"w":0.29012346903483077,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"c":1,"x":0.13156264000042767,"h":0.022134634855919599,"w":0.7759716288248697,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","y":0.17219211170105209},{"y":0.19316843319026078,"x":0.13168724180920205,"w":0.15843621571858729,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"t":"Passage 3 below."},{"y":0.22819767420454251,"w":0.50823043823242187,"t":"Why fairy tales are really scary tales","h":0.023274646350155193,"c":1,"x":0.27160494538636781},{"w":0.74300796508789058,"x":0.15422872977678992,"t":"Some people think that fairy tales are just stories to amuse children, but their","h":0.020448608308574201,"c":1,"y":0.26398122828310888},{"c":1,"w":0.65677591959635417,"x":0.19529354382223307,"h":0.023301644656627207,"t":"universal and enduring appeal may be due to more serious reasons","y":0.27933063439627648},{"h":0.019944666131225031,"x":0.12955359851377068,"c":1,"t":"People of every culture tell each other fairy tales but the same story often takes a variety of forms","y":0.3149136368971952,"w":0.78414138793945309},{"y":0.33173297845248284,"w":0.76766540527343752,"c":1,"x":0.12954185486587297,"t":"in different parts of the world. In the story of Little Red Riding Hood that European children are","h":0.019687356038986636},{"w":0.7636042277018229,"h":0.0200750431829122,"c":1,"t":"familiar with, a young girl on the way to see her grandmother meets a wolf and tells him where","y":0.34819456574601249,"x":0.1295210702669588},{"t":"she is going. The wolf runs on ahead and disposes of the grandmother, then gets into bed dressed","x":0.12956395503452039,"y":0.36593922819502367,"h":0.019224677967660142,"c":1,"w":0.77792953491210937},{"h":0.016022611984235047,"w":0.74897120157877595,"t":"in the grandmother's clothes to wait for Little Red Riding Hood. You may think you know the","y":0.38368669048096526,"c":1,"x":0.12962962552612661},{"w":0.74499542236328131,"c":1,"t":"story - but which version? In some versions, the wolf swallows up the grandmother, while in","y":0.39820102746732311,"x":0.12956231526158016,"h":0.019915394283155363},{"t":"others it locks her in a cupboard. In some stories Red Riding Hood gets the better of the wolf on","c":1,"x":0.13158422037889561,"y":0.41524073500918557,"h":0.02033935250326091,"w":0.7697710673014323},{"y":0.42904097041109501,"h":0.023661318038742718,"x":0.13152027841047603,"w":0.72043640136718756,"c":1,"t":"her own, while in others a hunter or a woodcutter hears her cries and comes to her rescue."},{"h":0.019950435355358231,"c":1,"t":"The universal appeal of these tales is frequently attributed to the idea that they contain cautionary","x":0.13158601359620975,"w":0.78003870646158835,"y":0.46464240064997897},{"h":0.02049089797955661,"t":"messages: in the case of Little Red Riding Hood, to listen to your mother, and avoid talking","w":0.7306740315755208,"y":0.48222584195008567,"x":0.13158087216300429,"c":1},{"t":"to strangers. 'It might be what we find interesting about this story is that it's got this survival-","w":0.7512091573079428,"y":0.49846364594838222,"h":0.019634197401354525,"c":1,"x":0.12953588481443204},{"y":0.51590106018512161,"h":0.017667844522968212,"w":0.75720163981119781,"x":0.12962963269534128,"c":1,"t":"relevant information in it,' says anthropologist Jamie Tehrani at Durham University in the UK."},{"h":0.019554600979610703,"t":"But his research suggests otherwise. 'We have this huge gap in our knowledge about the history","y":0.53188263258785951,"x":0.13160784640774523,"w":0.76765162150065103,"c":1},{"w":0.75543406168619798,"c":1,"x":0.13154319528395064,"h":0.02096552000730989,"t":"and prehistory of storytelling, despite the fact that we know this genre is an incredibly ancient","y":0.54773394533511632},{"x":0.13145514224928964,"y":0.56028082618175445,"c":1,"h":0.02755921187473831,"w":0.73703618367513013,"t":"one, he says. That hasn't stopped anthropologists, folklorists* and other academics devising"},{"y":0.58246923987159405,"w":0.76762690226236985,"x":0.13161912507728621,"t":"theories to explain the importance of fairy tales in human society. Now Tehrani has found a way","c":1,"h":0.018385450185679164},{"y":0.59995910379655271,"h":0.01868177330816867,"t":"to test these ideas, borrowing a technique from evolutionary biologists.","x":0.13158976222048485,"w":0.57219350179036454,"c":1},{"t":"To work out the evolutionary history, development and relationships among groups of organisms,","h":0.019074912908080055,"x":0.13161215335882806,"y":0.63190785350808509,"c":1,"w":0.78202916463216143},{"h":0.020156915392836372,"c":1,"y":0.64819653370036512,"w":0.78819101969401051,"t":"biologists compare the characteristics of living species in a process called 'phylogenetic analysis'.","x":0.13161896840005691},{"y":0.66554751017178382,"w":0.75530375162760433,"x":0.13161635240589922,"t":"Tehrani has used the same approach to compare related versions of fairy tales to discover how","c":1,"h":0.019939056414457035},{"t":"they have evolved and which elements have survived longest.","w":0.49396397908528644,"h":0.017651224304846225,"c":1,"x":0.13160910191766614,"y":0.68305585030940241},{"t":"Tehrani's analysis focused on Little Red Riding Hood in its many forms, which include another","y":0.7164310952962778,"x":0.13168723688046707,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"w":0.76131688435872391},{"y":0.73177784306702676,"t":"Western fairy tale known as The Wolf and the Kids. Checking for variants of these two tales and","h":0.019090178436890315,"c":1,"w":0.76566879272460941,"x":0.13363383578009158},{"y":0.74852768003685588,"x":0.13168723867654705,"c":1,"t":"similar stories from Africa, East Asia and other regions, he ended up with 58 stories recorded","w":0.74897120157877606,"h":0.018914180032215566},{"w":0.7820293680826822,"h":0.018795098236227714,"c":1,"t":"from oral traditions. Once his phylogenetic analysis had established that they were indeed related,","y":0.76559515670615375,"x":0.13366435305494567},{"y":0.78287084221049141,"x":0.13161841830412829,"h":0.017976849604270706,"t":"he used the same methods to explore how they have developed and altered over time.","w":0.68325317382812512,"c":1},{"h":0.019788299488656236,"x":0.1336517559222519,"c":1,"t":"First he tested some assumptions about which aspects of the story alter least as it evolves, indicating","w":0.78209264119466149,"y":0.81508227563290392},{"t":"their importance. Folklorists believe that what happens in a story is more centrai to the story","y":0.82994239722293683,"c":1,"x":0.13359384420985634,"h":0.022318310956651599,"w":0.72047368367513021},{"x":0.13366909361228002,"c":1,"t":"than the characters in it - that visiting a relative, only to be met by a scary animal in disguise, is","y":0.8485046880486028,"h":0.020354841567040594,"w":0.74707860310872376},{"y":0.89534883711370183,"h":0.010174418787512574,"x":0.13580246306333521,"w":0.26131688435872397,"c":1,"t":"Folklorists: those who study traditional stories"},{"w":0.024691357612609877,"y":0.91569767424158999,"t":"66","x":0.13374485607959105,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1}],"w":2400}